      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17012162_0076.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140424_17012162_0076&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17012162_0076.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17012925_0077.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140424_17012925_0077&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140424_17012925_0077.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: S.R.A., To: Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Postcard Info: Collett Park, Terre Haute, Ind.&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Terre Haute, Indiana on May 23, 1911&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
253 N. Estille Ave.&lt;br&gt;
Wichita, Kansas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terre Haute 5/22/11&lt;br&gt;
Friend Ruby,&lt;br&gt;
Your card received and credited to the sender. To be sure, it was appropriate in a sense. Hope and pray that you are enjoying life among the sunflowers. I think others are missed also in Pearl, the first. Would like to hear from you.&lt;br&gt;
S.R.A&lt;br&gt;
931 North Place&lt;/p&gt;</description>
